Files under crates/vmm/src/{vstate,arch,devices,builder} are derived from
Firecracker's src/vmm crate as of its main branch on 2026-10-10: upstream
commit fd9fc7a9f164b73002d22065d17c150d8c262d91 (2026-10-08), the newest on
main at the port. Upstream's security advisories up to then are in that tree;
the two published in 2026 (GHSA-776c-mpj7-jm3r, the virtio-pci transport, and
GHSA-36j2-f825-qvgc, the jailer) are in code this port does not carry. A later
upstream fix is taken by comparing against that commit. crates/vmm/src/builder.rs
additionally from Firecracker's src/device_manager/legacy.rs (outside src/vmm),
and adapted:

- trimmed to the multi-VM spawner base: removed metrics, the in-crate logger,
  seccomp, event-manager, mmds, pci, gdb, vhost-user,
  rate-limiter, balloon, block/net virtio devices and the api-server;
- error types re-derived with thiserror; Firecracker-internal log and metric
  macros removed;
- added spawner module (N-VM lifecycle) and hvf module (Apple Silicon
  Hypervisor.framework backend, not present upstream).

Files under crates/vmm/src/devices/virtio/ are derived from Firecracker's
src/vmm crate in part, and written for this port in part:

- crates/vmm/src/devices/virtio/mmio.rs is derived from Firecracker
  src/vmm/src/devices/virtio/transport/mmio.rs and
  src/vmm/src/devices/virtio/device.rs (Apache-2.0, Copyright 2018
  Amazon.com, Inc. or its affiliates): the virtio-mmio register set, the
  driver status state machine, the feature-page selection and the
  interrupt-status handling are upstream's, trimmed to this port's needs (no
  event manager, no metrics, no userspace virtqueue processing, a
  `Box<dyn VirtioDevice>` instead of `Arc<Mutex<dyn VirtioDevice>>`, and a
  `VirtioDevice` trait of this port's own that also carries the device
  configuration space, which upstream reads through its queue machinery).
- crates/vmm/src/devices/virtio/vhost_device.rs and
  crates/vmm/src/devices/virtio/vhost.rs are written for this port
  (Copyright 2026 AgentPlaza, Apache-2.0). `vhost.rs` is the binding to the
  host kernel's `/dev/vhost-vsock` stack — the ioctl sequence and memory table
  QEMU's `vhost_dev_init`/`vhost_virtqueue_start` perform — reimplemented from
  the kernel's `include/uapi/linux/vhost.h` and `drivers/vhost/vsock.c`; the
  `vhost` crate Firecracker uses for this interface is not a dependency of
  this tree, and no code was copied from Firecracker, QEMU or that crate for
  it. `vhost_device.rs` is the virtio-mmio wrapper around that backend. Both
  are now **retired**: the boot path uses the userspace vsock device (above),
  and nothing constructs `VsockDevice` or opens `/dev/vhost-vsock`. They
  survive only for their tests and for the `ack_feature_page`/
  `read_guest_cid_config` helpers the userspace device's `mmio_device`
  adapter reuses.
  What was measured on real hardware is recorded in
  crates/vmm/src/devices/virtio/FACTS.md.

- crates/vmm/src/devices/virtio/queue.rs, iovec.rs, iov_deque.rs,
  test_utils.rs and vsock/{mod,packet,device,metrics}.rs are derived from
  Firecracker's src/vmm/src/devices/virtio/{queue.rs,iovec.rs,iov_deque.rs,
  test_utils.rs,vsock/{mod,packet,device,metrics}.rs} (Apache-2.0, Copyright
  2018-2024 Amazon.com, Inc. or its affiliates): the userspace virtqueue
  processing core (descriptor-chain walking, used/avail rings), the
  scatter/gather iovec buffers, the virtio-vsock packet model and the
  userspace vsock device frontend (the `VsockChannel`/`VsockEpollListener`/
  `VsockBackend` interface and `Vsock<B>`). Trimmed to this port's needs:
  the event-manager is dropped (the snapshot state is this port's own
  `save_device_state`/`restore_device_state`, see the snapshot note below), `displaydoc`
  becomes explicit `thiserror` messages, the `memfd` crate becomes raw `libc`
  calls, and Firecracker's metrics become a local no-op atomic shim.

- crates/vmm/src/devices/virtio/vsock/csm/{mod,connection,txbuf}.rs and
  vsock/unix/{mod,muxer,muxer_killq,muxer_rxq}.rs are derived from Firecracker
  src/vmm/src/devices/virtio/vsock/{csm/{mod,connection,txbuf},unix/
  {mod,muxer,muxer_killq,muxer_rxq}}.rs (Apache-2.0, Copyright 2018-2024
  Amazon.com, Inc. or its affiliates): the vsock connection state machine
  (`VsockConnection`), its TX ring buffer, and the Unix-domain-socket
  multiplexer (`VsockMuxer`) that mediates guest AF_VSOCK connections to
  host AF_UNIX sockets. Trimmed to this port's needs: the event-manager
  scaffolding is dropped, `displaydoc` becomes explicit `thiserror` messages,
  `crate::logger`/`crate::utils` are folded into local helpers, and
  `debug!`/`info!` calls are removed while `warn!`/`error!` become
  `eprintln!`.

  The test modules are also upstream's, adapted: the `tests` module of
  `src/vmm/src/devices/virtio/vsock/csm/connection.rs` (all 18 cases: the
  connection-request handshake, the shutdown matrix, the credit-request/
  credit-update paths, TX buffering, stream write errors, and the EPOLLIN/
  EPOLLOUT starvation regressions) and the packet assembly/accessor/bounds
  cases of `vsock/packet.rs` are ported. Upstream's event-manager test harness
  (`TestContext` + `create_event_handler_context`) is replaced by this port's
  `VirtQueue` (which lays the descriptor chains out in guest memory directly),
  `crate::vstate::memory::BitmapSlice` becomes `vm_memory::bitmap::BitmapSlice`,
  and the `csm_defs` alias is dropped in favour of `csm::defs`; the assertions
  and the cases themselves are unchanged.

- crates/vmm/src/devices/virtio/vsock/{event_thread,mmio_device}.rs and
  crates/vmm/src/sys.rs are written for this port (Copyright 2026 AgentPlaza,
  Apache-2.0): the per-VM vsock event thread (replacing Firecracker's
  event-manager subscriber, including upstream's per-event `is_activated()`
  re-check), the `VirtioDevice` adapter that bridges the mmio transport's
  `QueueConfig` to the userspace device's real virtqueues, and the crate's
  raw-syscall boundary (`poll(2)`, `uname(2)`, and the non-blocking
  `socket(2)`+`connect(2)` pair). One function of that boundary,
  `sys::connect_unix_nonblocking`, is Firecracker's
  `VsockMuxer::connect_nonblocking` from
  src/vmm/src/devices/virtio/vsock/unix/muxer.rs (Apache-2.0, Copyright 2018
  Amazon.com, Inc. or its affiliates), moved into this port's syscall boundary
  and adapted only in its error reporting: the socket is created non-blocking
  *before* `connect(2)`, so a full listener backlog is `EAGAIN` rather than a
  blocked caller. The muxer's call site delegates to it.

- crates/vmm/src/devices/virtio/block/{mod,device,request,test_utils}.rs are
  derived from Firecracker's src/vmm/src/devices/virtio/block/virtio/{mod.rs,
  device.rs, request.rs, test_utils.rs} and
  src/vmm/src/devices/virtio/block/virtio/io/sync_io.rs (Apache-2.0, Copyright
  2018-2021 Amazon.com, Inc. or its affiliates; upstream commit
  fd9fc7a9f164b73002d22065d17c150d8c262d91 of firecracker-microvm/firecracker):
  the virtio-blk device model, its request parsers and the synchronous
  file-engine transfer that backs them.

  Ported unchanged in behaviour: `RequestHeader`, `RequestType`, `Request::parse`
  and `Request::validate_discard_ranges` (every bounds check, every error case
  and every descriptor-direction rule), the `Status`/`PendingRequest`/
  `FinishedRequest` status-byte protocol, `DiskProperties` (the backing file and
  the `virtio_blk_config` configuration space), and `VirtioBlk::process_queue`'s
  loop (pop, parse, execute, `add_used`, `advance_used_ring_idx`,
  `prepare_kick`). The test modules of `request.rs` and `test_utils.rs` are
  upstream's cases, adapted (`RequestDescriptorChain` now publishes its three
  descriptors into this port's `VirtQueue` instead of upstream's per-descriptor
  cells, and upstream's proptest matrix is not ported because the port takes no
  `proptest` dependency).

  Local modifications, marked in the files' headers:
  * trimmed — the async io_uring engine (`io/async_io.rs`), the rate limiter,
    the device metrics, upstream's persist module (the queue positions are saved
    through this port's own device snapshot hooks instead), the event-manager
    subscriber and its queue/interrupt event fds, the PCI transport,
    multi-queue, read-only drives, `CacheType`, and DISCARD/WRITE_ZEROES
    execution (their `fallocate`/`BLKDISCARD` ioctls are `unsafe` and a writable
    workspace does not need them; a discard request is answered
    `VIRTIO_BLK_S_UNSUPP`, which upstream also does when the feature is not
    negotiated);
  * the request header and the discard range are read as little-endian
    `zerocopy` fields instead of upstream's platform-endian `ByteValued` PODs —
    no `unsafe impl` under this port's safe-Rust policy, and correct on any
    host endianness;
  * `displaydoc` derives become explicit `thiserror` messages and
    `crate::logger` calls become `eprintln!`;
  * `GET_ID` answers with zeroes instead of upstream's file metadata: host
    information must not reach a guest (plaza invariant 2);
  * the device is synchronous (no event thread): it serves its queue inside the
    MMIO transport's notification, and it fsyncs on a flush request.

- crates/vmm/src/devices/virtio/block/mmio_device.rs is written for this port
