The Apache License, Version 2.0 text is in crates/vmm/LICENSE.

Snapshots are ported from Firecracker, not left out of this tree. The snapshot state of the VM, its vCPUs and its
devices (`VmState`, `VcpuState` and the virtio transport and queue state, from Firecracker's `src/vmm/src/persist.rs`,
`arch/*` and the device persist code) is Firecracker's, and so is the sequence of a snapshot: pause the vCPUs, save
their state, the VM's and the devices', dump the memory, resume (`crates/vmm/src/control.rs`, from `create_snapshot`).
The vCPU pause and resume run loop is Firecracker's too (`crates/vmm/src/vstate/vcpu.rs`). Both are Apache-2.0,
Copyright 2018-2025 Amazon.com, Inc. or its affiliates. The on-disk layout (`crates/vmm/src/vstate/snapshot.rs`), the
version and architecture checks, and the device gate are this port's own, Copyright 2026 AgentPlaza, Apache-2.0.

The page selection for diffs (`crates/vmm/src/vstate/snapshot_memory.rs`) follows CubeSandbox's
`hypervisor/vmm/src/pagemap_anon.rs` (Apache-2.0, Copyright Tencent): a diff writes the anonymous pages of a restored VM,
found through `/proc/self/pagemap`. The code is this port's own; the selection rule is theirs.

