crates/vmm/src/jail/{jailer.rs,jailer_sys.rs} are written for this port
(Copyright 2026 AgentPlaza, Apache-2.0): the VMM's jailer. Its shape follows
Firecracker's `src/jailer` crate (Apache-2.0, Copyright 2018 Amazon.com, Inc.
or its affiliates) — src/chroot.rs's mount namespace, bind-over-itself,
`pivot_root`, `chdir("/")` and lazy unmount of the old root, and src/env.rs's
`/dev` nodes and uid/gid drop — but no code was copied: this port's VMMs are
threads inside `noded`/`vmctl` rather than a program that forks and `exec`s a
VMM child, so the jailer is an in-process step on the VMM's own thread, with no
control plane, no cgroup, no netns, no daemonize and no `exec`. The bind/syscall
wrappers are reimplemented against the Linux UAPI headers. See
crates/vmm/src/jail/jailer.rs for the shape, the post-pivot path audit and the
namespaces deliberately not used.
